<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dakota people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dakota are a Siouan-speaking Indigenous people, one of the main divisions of the Oceti Sakowin, or Seven Council Fires, often called the Sioux. The eastern Dakota, or Santee, lived around the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minnesota">Minnesota</a> rivers, where they hunted, fished and gathered wild <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>. After the Dakota War of 1862 in Minnesota many were expelled to reservations further west, and Dakota communities live today in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</p></div>
